# ghalbol_core owns product logic

**`ghalbol_core` (Rust)** owns crypto, text delivery, calls, outbox, acks, contacts, transcripts, invites, OS network truth, and coord/bridge policy.

**`ghalbol_app` (Makepad 2)** is the only UI. It links `ghalbol_core` and calls **`ghalbol_core::host`** in-process. Splash is `script_mod!`. Where Makepad 2 lacks a widget or platform affordance, complete the behaviour in Splash. See `docs/MAKEPAD_UI.md`.

When adding features (including connectivity, acks, storage):

- Implement behaviour in **`ghalbol_core`** and call it from **`ghalbol_core::host`**.
- Keep the UI in-process via `host` — do not add a second language binding or out-of-process RPC for the Makepad app.
- The Makepad app polls and displays native state. Do not duplicate OS probes in the UI.
- Do not move ack policy, outbox, transcript merge, or WAN/LAN dial policy into Splash.

See `AGENTS.md` and `docs/DESIGN.md` for the full split.

Never rename protocol or storage strings (Noise prologue, HKDF / AAD info, signing domains, `ghalbol.share` values, mDNS service, on-disk folder names) as a cleanup — it breaks every existing peer, server and keystore. The legacy `ghal_bol` constants in `keystore_v1.rs` and `app_paths.rs` exist on purpose. CI denies warnings on Linux, Windows and Android (`scripts/check_android.sh`).
